{"id":"alps-passes-moto","title":"Alpine passes: Stelvio, Gavia and Grossglockner","who":"Classic route · the great passes by motorcycle","when":"June to September (passes closed in winter)","vehicle":"Motorcycle, 6–8 days","kind":"moto","color":"#e11d48","summary":"The legendary roads of the Alps: the Stelvio's 48 hairpins, the narrow Gavia, the Bernina into Switzerland, the Timmelsjoch, and Austria's Grossglockner High Alpine Road under the country's highest peak, with the Dolomites in between. Ride early to beat the crowds.","sources":[{"label":"Rider Magazine: Edelweiss Grand Alps tour review (January 2025)","url":"https://ridermagazine.com/2025/01/29/edelweiss-grand-alps-tour-review/"},{"label":"Motovibes: 8-day Central Alps challenge","url":"https://motovibes-shop.fourthwall.com/products/8-day-central-alps-challenge-self-guided-motorcycle-tour"}],"approximate":"A common loop; the roads are the router's choice.","km":682,"bbox":[10.0276,46.3435,12.9131,47.0388],"stops":[{"name":"Bormio","place":"Bormio, Italy","at":[46.4677,10.3775],"text":"The base for the two great passes.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/BORMIO_panoramica.jpg/500px-BORMIO_panoramica.jpg","page":"Bormio","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BORMIO_panoramica.jpg","credit":"Sauro Sisti","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Stelvio Pass","place":"Passo dello Stelvio","at":[46.5286,10.4532],"text":"48 numbered hairpins on the Trafoi side up to 2,757 m.","source":{"label":"Rider Magazine (2025)","url":"https://ridermagazine.com/2025/01/29/edelweiss-grand-alps-tour-review/"}},{"name":"Gavia Pass","place":"Passo di Gavia","at":[46.3435,10.4873],"text":"A narrow, wild road over 2,621 m, famous from the Giro d'Italia.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Passo_del_Gavia.jpg/500px-Passo_del_Gavia.jpg","page":"Gavia Pass","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Passo_del_Gavia.jpg","credit":"Gabri80 at